const body = `<h1>2D Arrays: Quick Reference</h1>

<p>One page, no story, no lab. The shapes, signatures, and traps of the unit,
compressed. This is the page to keep open during builds and to re-read the
night before a test. Print it and mark it up.</p>

<h2>Creation</h2>
<pre><code>int[][] grid = new int[4][5];      // 4 rows, 5 cols, all 0
int[][] m = {{1,2,3},{4,5,6}};     // 2 rows, 3 cols
char[][] map = new char[rows][];   // jagged: rows first, fill later</code></pre>

<h2>Dimensions</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Expression</th><th>Is</th></tr>
    <tr><td>grid.length</td><td>the number of ROWS</td></tr>
    <tr><td>grid[r].length</td><td>the length of row r (columns, if rectangular)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>grid[r][c]</td><td>the cell at row r, column c</td></tr>
</table>


<h2>The Walks</h2>
<pre><code>// row-major (the default)
for (int r = 0; r &lt; grid.length; r++)
    for (int c = 0; c &lt; grid[r].length; c++)
        visit(grid[r][c]);

// column-major
for (int c = 0; c &lt; grid[0].length; c++)
    for (int r = 0; r &lt; grid.length; r++)
        visit(grid[r][c]);</code></pre>

<h2>Neighbors (4-directional)</h2>
<pre><code>if (r &gt; 0)                  check grid[r-1][c]   // up
if (r &lt; grid.length-1)       check grid[r+1][c]   // down
if (c &gt; 0)                  check grid[r][c-1]   // left
if (c &lt; grid[r].length-1)   check grid[r][c+1]   // right</code></pre>

<h2>Box traversal (bounded)</h2>
<pre><code>for (int r = Math.max(0, r1); r &lt;= Math.min(grid.length-1, r2); r++)
    for (int c = Math.max(0, c1); c &lt;= Math.min(grid[r].length-1, c2); c++)
        visit(grid[r][c]);</code></pre>


<h2>The Unit's Traps, One Line Each</h2>
<ul>
    <li>grid.length is ROWS. Row-first thinking: [row][col], always.</li>
    <li>Jagged rows are legal. Use grid[r].length per row; a width constant breaks.</li>
    <li>Swapped bounds compile on square grids and crash on rectangles. Match variable to bound.</li>
    <li>Negative indices do not exist. Bounds checks BEFORE access, every neighbor, every time.</li>
</ul>

<h2>See Also</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a href="../unit-08/2d-array-basics.html">2D Array Basics</a></li>
    <li><a href="../unit-08/2d-array-traversal.html">2D Array Traversal</a></li>
    <li><a href="../unit-08/2d-algorithms.html">2D Array Algorithms</a></li>
    <li><a href="../unit-08/neighbors-boundaries.html">Neighbors &amp; Boundaries</a></li>
    <li><a href="../unit-08/maps-from-files.html">Maps From Files</a></li>
</ul>`;
